Harmattan: a read-only Tracker 0.10 contacts engine, the default manager

The phone keeps its address book in Tracker (the nco ontology; Nokia's Qt 4 plugin was
qtcontacts-tracker, for Qt Mobility). This engine, "tracker", reads the people the address
book shows (nco:PersonContact, without the owner's nco:default-contact-me card): names,
nickname, a display label, phone numbers with their subtypes and e-mail addresses, the
person's own (home context) and their affiliation's (work context). Five plain SPARQL queries
over org.freedesktop.Tracker1.Resources.SparqlQuery, joined on the contact's IRI; every
class and property was checked against the phone's 32-nco.ontology. Filters and sort orders
are applied in memory with the base engine's testFilter/addSorted, so all of them work;
fetch requests complete inside startRequest, as the memory engine's do. Saving, removing,
relationships and collections are refused. Tracker's GraphUpdated on an nco class emits
dataChanged().

Q_CONTACTS_DEFAULT_ENGINE makes it the manager QContactManager() opens. Apps need Aegis'
TrackerReadAccess credential: without it Tracker refuses the query (PermissionsError).

